module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineTransitionLimit
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Affine
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LimitUniverse.AffineTransitionLimit

/-!
# Affineness over the base descends to a finite stage

Let `D` be a cofiltered diagram of quasi-compact and quasi-separated schemes with affine
transition morphisms, let `S` be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme, and let
`t : D ⟶ (Functor.const _).obj S` exhibit every stage as an `S`-scheme. If the induced morphism
`f : lim D ⟶ S` is affine, then `t.app i` is affine for every sufficiently late stage `i`.

This is Stacks Tag 09ZM.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.EventuallyAffine.map_comp_app` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.EventuallyAffine.isAffineHom_app_of_hom`: naturality of a transformation to
  a constant diagram, and the resulting propagation of affineness to later stages.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineHom_app_of_isLimit`: there is a stage at which the structure
  morphism to `S` is affine.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.eventually_isAffineHom_of_isLimit`: the structure morphism is affine at
  *every* stage admitting a morphism to that one, which is Tag 09ZM in the form "for `i` large
  enough".
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineHom_app_of_isLimit_of_initiallySmall` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.eventually_isAffineHom_of_isLimit_of_initiallySmall`: the same two results
  with the index universes independent of the scheme universe, at the cost of
  `CategoryTheory.LocallySmall` and `CategoryTheory.InitiallySmall` on the index category.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.eventually_isAffineHom_of_isLimit_of_essentiallySmall`: the same under the
  single hypothesis `CategoryTheory.EssentiallySmall.{u} I`.

## Implementation notes

The proof is the Stacks proof. `S` is quasi-compact, so it has a finite cover by affine opens
`V`. Fix a stage `i₀`. The inverse image `U_V := (t.app i₀) ⁻¹ᵁ V` is a quasi-compact open of
`D.obj i₀`, because a morphism from a quasi-compact scheme to a quasi-separated scheme is
quasi-compact; its inverse image in the limit is `f ⁻¹ᵁ V`, which is affine since `f` is. By
`AlgebraicGeometry.isLimitOpensCone` the inverse images of `U_V` at the stages over `i₀` form an
inverse system whose limit is `f ⁻¹ᵁ V`, so Tag 01Z6
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_isAffine_of_isLimit`) produces a stage over `i₀` at which the
inverse image of `U_V` is affine. Cofilteredness merges the finitely many stages so obtained into
one stage `i`, at which `(t.app i) ⁻¹ᵁ V` is affine for every `V` in the cover — an affine open
is pulled back to an affine open along the affine transition morphisms — and affineness of a
morphism is local on the target. Finally `t.app j = D.map g ≫ t.app i` for `g : j ⟶ i`, and a
composite of affine morphisms is affine, which gives the "sufficiently late" form for free.

## The index universe, and the smallness hypothesis

Tag 09ZM inherits its hypotheses from Situation 086P, which takes "a directed system of schemes
with affine transition morphisms (Lemma 01YX)", and Tag 01YX opens "Let `I` be a directed set".
The index is therefore a *set*, and a statement of 09ZM with an index category `I : Type uI`
carrying no smallness condition relative to the scheme universe `u` has dropped a hypothesis the
source has. Such a statement is false, so the results below carry the smallness condition.

The weakest form available is used: the index universes are left free of the scheme universe, and
`CategoryTheory.LocallySmall.{u} I` together with `CategoryTheory.InitiallySmall.{u} I` are
assumed. Those are exactly the hypotheses under which
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/LimitUniverse/AffineTransitionLimit.lean` makes Mathlib's limit
API — which is stated only for `I : Type u` with `[Category.{u} I]` — available at an independent
index universe. `CategoryTheory.EssentiallySmall.{u} I` implies both (and
`I : Type u` with `[Category.{u} I]` implies that in turn), so the merged-universe form is a
special case; for a thin index `CategoryTheory.locallySmall_of_thin` discharges the first
hypothesis and only `CategoryTheory.InitiallySmall.{u} I` remains.

Neither hypothesis is vacuous. `Ordinal.{u}` is a nonempty directed preorder no `u`-small subset
of which is cofinal, so `CategoryTheory.InitiallySmall.{u} (Ordinal.{u})ᵒᵖ` is false, and
`(Ordinal.{u})ᵒᵖ` is a legal index for a diagram of `Scheme.{u}`. For 09ZM specifically the
smallness is load-bearing and not merely an artefact of the route. Let `F` be a field with
`¬ Small.{u} F`, index on `I := (Finset F)ᵒᵖ`, and for a finite `T ⊆ F` let `A T` be a `Type u`
model of the subring of `F` generated by `T` — finitely generated, hence countable, hence
`u`-small. Let the stage at `T` be the quasi-compact open `D(x) ∪ D(y)` of `Spec (A T)[x, y]`,
with transition morphisms induced by the inclusions `A T' ⊆ A T`, and let `S := Spec ℤ` with `t`
the terminal morphisms. Transition morphisms are affine, every stage is quasi-compact and
quasi-separated, and `S` is affine. The limit of this diagram is the *empty* scheme: a cone with
vertex `Z` gives, on global sections, a compatible family of ring maps `(A T)[x, y] ⟶ Γ(Z, ⊤)`,
hence a compatible family `A T ⟶ Γ(Z, ⊤)`; as every element of `F` lies in some `A T` these
assemble into a ring map `F ⟶ Γ(Z, ⊤)`, injective unless `Γ(Z, ⊤) = 0` because `F` is a field,
and injectivity would make `F` be `u`-small. So `Γ(Z, ⊤) = 0`, i.e. `Z = ∅`, and the empty scheme
with its unique morphisms is a limiting cone. The induced morphism `∅ ⟶ S` is affine, the inverse
image of any affine open being `∅`. But `t.app T` is affine at no stage: `S` is affine, so that
would force `D(x) ∪ D(y) ⊆ Spec (A T)[x, y]` to be affine, and it is not — its ring of global
sections is `(A T)[x, y]` while the open immersion into `Spec (A T)[x, y]` is not surjective,
`A T` being a nonzero ring.

The analysis for the sibling tags 06AC and 09ZN is in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Limits/DescendingMorphisms/FiniteLocallyFree.lean` and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/EventualFiniteness/Basic.lean`.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Tag 09ZM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09ZM)
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 01Z6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Z6)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.InitiallySmall

universe v uI u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace EventuallyAffine

variable {I : Type uI} [Category.{v} I] {S : Scheme.{u}} {D : I ⥤ Scheme.{u}}

/-- The structure morphisms of an `S`-diagram are compatible with its transition morphisms. -/
lemma map_comp_app (t : D ⟶ (Functor.const I).obj S) {i j : I} (g : i ⟶ j) :
    D.map g ≫ (t.app j : D.obj j ⟶ S) = (t.app i : D.obj i ⟶ S) := by
  simp

/-- The structure morphism of a stage is affine as soon as it is affine at some earlier stage. -/
lemma isAffineHom_app_of_hom (t : D ⟶ (Functor.const I).obj S)
    [∀ {i j : I} (g : i ⟶ j), IsAffineHom (D.map g)] {i j : I}
    (g : j ⟶ i) (hi : IsAffineHom (t.app i)) : IsAffineHom (t.app j) := by
  rw [← map_comp_app t g]
  infer_instance

end EventuallyAffine

section Small

variable {I : Type u} [Category.{u} I] [IsCofiltered I] {S : Scheme.{u}}
  [CompactSpace S] [QuasiSeparatedSpace S]

/-- **Stacks Tag 09ZM**, in the form "there is a stage at which the structure morphism is
affine". The index category lives in the universe of the schemes; see
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineHom_app_of_isLimit_of_initiallySmall` for the version with
independent index universes, and the module documentation for why no condition at all on the
index category will do. -/
theorem exists_isAffineHom_app_of_isLimit (D : I ⥤ Scheme.{u})
    (t : D ⟶ (Functor.const I).obj S) (c : Cone D) (hc : IsLimit c) (f : c.pt ⟶ S)
    (hf : c.π ≫ t = (Functor.const I).map f)
    [∀ i, CompactSpace (D.obj i)] [∀ i, QuasiSeparatedSpace (D.obj i)]
    [∀ {i j : I} (g : i ⟶ j), IsAffineHom (D.map g)] [IsAffineHom f] :
    ∃ i : I, IsAffineHom (t.app i) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨i₀⟩ := IsCofiltered.nonempty (C := I)
  have hπt : ∀ i : I, c.π.app i ≫ t.app i = f := fun i ↦ by
    simpa using NatTrans.congr_app hf i
  have hmem : ∀ x : S, ∃ V : S.affineOpens, x ∈ (V : Set S) := fun x ↦ by
    obtain ⟨_, ⟨V, hV, rfl⟩, hxV, -⟩ :=
      S.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ x) isOpen_univ
    exact ⟨⟨V, hV⟩, hxV⟩
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := isCompact_univ.elim_finite_subcover
    (fun V : S.affineOpens ↦ (V : Set S)) (fun V ↦ V.1.2)
    fun x _ ↦ Set.mem_iUnion.2 (hmem x)
  have key : ∀ V : S.affineOpens, ∃ (j : I) (g : j ⟶ i₀),
      IsAffineOpen (D.map g ⁻¹ᵁ t.app i₀ ⁻¹ᵁ (V : S.Opens)) := by
    intro V
    set U : (D.obj i₀).Opens := t.app i₀ ⁻¹ᵁ (V : S.Opens) with hU
    have : QuasiSeparatedSpace (((Functor.const I).obj S).obj i₀) := ‹_›
    have hUc : IsCompact (U : Set (D.obj i₀)) :=
      QuasiCompact.isCompact_preimage (f := t.app i₀) _ V.1.2 V.2.isCompact
    have hcomp (a : Over i₀) : CompactSpace ((opensDiagram D i₀ U).obj a) :=
      isCompact_iff_compactSpace.mp
        (QuasiCompact.isCompact_preimage (f := D.map a.hom) _ U.2 hUc)
    have hqs (a : Over i₀) : QuasiSeparatedSpace ((opensDiagram D i₀ U).obj a) :=
      (isQuasiSeparated_iff_quasiSeparatedSpace _ (D.map a.hom ⁻¹ᵁ U).2).mp
        (.of_quasiSeparatedSpace _)
    have haff : IsAffine (opensCone D c i₀ U).pt := by
      change IsAffine (c.π.app i₀ ⁻¹ᵁ U).toScheme
      rw [hU, ← Scheme.Hom.comp_preimage, hπt i₀]
      exact V.2.preimage f
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ :=
      Scheme.exists_isAffine_of_isLimit _ _ (isLimitOpensCone D c hc i₀ U)
    exact ⟨a.left, a.hom, ha⟩
  choose j g hj using key
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := IsCofiltered.inf_objs_exists (σ.image j)
  replace hi : ∀ V ∈ σ, i ⟶ j V := fun V hV ↦ (hi (Finset.mem_image_of_mem j hV)).some
  refine ⟨i, isAffineHom_of_forall_exists_isAffineOpen (t.app i) fun x ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨V, hVσ, hxV⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (hσ (Set.mem_univ x))
  refine ⟨(V : S.Opens), hxV, V.2, ?_⟩
  rw [← EventuallyAffine.map_comp_app t (hi V hVσ ≫ g V), Scheme.Hom.comp_preimage, D.map_comp,
    Scheme.Hom.comp_preimage]
  exact (hj V).preimage (D.map (hi V hVσ))

/-- **Stacks Tag 09ZM.** Let `lim D` be a cofiltered limit of quasi-compact and quasi-separated
schemes over a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme `S`, with affine transition morphisms. If
the induced morphism `lim D ⟶ S` is affine, then `D.obj j ⟶ S` is affine for every sufficiently
late stage `j`.

The index category lives in the universe of the schemes; see
`AlgebraicGeometry.eventually_isAffineHom_of_isLimit_of_initiallySmall` for the version with
independent index universes, and the module documentation for why no condition at all on the
index category will do. -/
@[sga "4 VII 5.4" "affine clause, partial"]
theorem eventually_isAffineHom_of_isLimit (D : I ⥤ Scheme.{u})
    (t : D ⟶ (Functor.const I).obj S) (c : Cone D) (hc : IsLimit c) (f : c.pt ⟶ S)
    (hf : c.π ≫ t = (Functor.const I).map f)
    [∀ i, CompactSpace (D.obj i)] [∀ i, QuasiSeparatedSpace (D.obj i)]
    [∀ {i j : I} (g : i ⟶ j), IsAffineHom (D.map g)] [IsAffineHom f] :
    ∃ i : I, ∀ {j : I} (_ : j ⟶ i), IsAffineHom (t.app j) := by
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := exists_isAffineHom_app_of_isLimit D t c hc f hf
  exact ⟨i, fun g ↦ EventuallyAffine.isAffineHom_app_of_hom t g hi⟩

end Small

section InitiallySmall

variable {I : Type uI} [Category.{v} I] [IsCofiltered I]
  [LocallySmall.{u} I] [InitiallySmall.{u} I]
  {S : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace S] [QuasiSeparatedSpace S]

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineHom_app_of_isLimit` with the index universes independent of
the scheme universe, at the cost of `CategoryTheory.LocallySmall.{u}` and
`CategoryTheory.InitiallySmall.{u}` on the index category. See the module documentation for why
some such condition is necessary. -/
theorem exists_isAffineHom_app_of_isLimit_of_initiallySmall (D : I ⥤ Scheme.{u})
    (t : D ⟶ (Functor.const I).obj S) (c : Cone D) (hc : IsLimit c) (f : c.pt ⟶ S)
    (hf : c.π ≫ t = (Functor.const I).map f)
    [∀ i, CompactSpace (D.obj i)] [∀ i, QuasiSeparatedSpace (D.obj i)]
    [∀ {i j : I} (g : i ⟶ j), IsAffineHom (D.map g)] [IsAffineHom f] :
    ∃ i : I, IsAffineHom (t.app i) := by
  set A := CofilteredInitialModel.{u} I
  set φ : A ⥤ I := fromCofilteredInitialModel.{u} I with hφ
  let D' : A ⥤ Scheme.{u} := φ ⋙ D
  let t' : D' ⟶ (Functor.const A).obj S :=
    { app a := t.app (φ.obj a)
      naturality a b h := by simp [D'] }
  have h₁ : ∀ {a b : A} (h : a ⟶ b), IsAffineHom (D'.map h) := by
    intros; dsimp [D']; infer_instance
  have h₂ : ∀ a : A, CompactSpace (D'.obj a) := by intro a; dsimp [D']; infer_instance
  have h₃ : ∀ a : A, QuasiSeparatedSpace (D'.obj a) := by intro a; dsimp [D']; infer_instance
  have hc' : IsLimit (c.whisker φ) := (Functor.Initial.isLimitWhiskerEquiv φ c).symm hc
  have hf' : (c.whisker φ).π ≫ t' = (Functor.const A).map f := by
    ext a
    simpa [t'] using NatTrans.congr_app hf (φ.obj a)
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := exists_isAffineHom_app_of_isLimit D' t' _ hc' f hf'
  exact ⟨φ.obj a, ha⟩

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.eventually_isAffineHom_of_isLimit` with the index universes independent
of the scheme universe, at the cost of `CategoryTheory.LocallySmall.{u}` and
`CategoryTheory.InitiallySmall.{u}` on the index category. See the module documentation for why
some such condition is necessary. -/
@[stacks 09ZM]
theorem eventually_isAffineHom_of_isLimit_of_initiallySmall (D : I ⥤ Scheme.{u})
    (t : D ⟶ (Functor.const I).obj S) (c : Cone D) (hc : IsLimit c) (f : c.pt ⟶ S)
    (hf : c.π ≫ t = (Functor.const I).map f)
    [∀ i, CompactSpace (D.obj i)] [∀ i, QuasiSeparatedSpace (D.obj i)]
    [∀ {i j : I} (g : i ⟶ j), IsAffineHom (D.map g)] [IsAffineHom f] :
    ∃ i : I, ∀ {j : I} (_ : j ⟶ i), IsAffineHom (t.app j) := by
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := exists_isAffineHom_app_of_isLimit_of_initiallySmall D t c hc f hf
  exact ⟨i, fun g ↦ EventuallyAffine.isAffineHom_app_of_hom t g hi⟩

end InitiallySmall

section EssentiallySmall

variable {I : Type uI} [Category.{v} I] [IsCofiltered I] [EssentiallySmall.{u} I]
  {S : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace S] [QuasiSeparatedSpace S]

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.eventually_isAffineHom_of_isLimit_of_initiallySmall` under the single
hypothesis `CategoryTheory.EssentiallySmall.{u} I`, which implies the pair of hypotheses of that
version. -/
theorem eventually_isAffineHom_of_isLimit_of_essentiallySmall (D : I ⥤ Scheme.{u})
    (t : D ⟶ (Functor.const I).obj S) (c : Cone D) (hc : IsLimit c) (f : c.pt ⟶ S)
    (hf : c.π ≫ t = (Functor.const I).map f)
    [∀ i, CompactSpace (D.obj i)] [∀ i, QuasiSeparatedSpace (D.obj i)]
    [∀ {i j : I} (g : i ⟶ j), IsAffineHom (D.map g)] [IsAffineHom f] :
    ∃ i : I, ∀ {j : I} (_ : j ⟶ i), IsAffineHom (t.app j) :=
  have : InitiallySmall.{u} I := initiallySmall_of_essentiallySmall I
  eventually_isAffineHom_of_isLimit_of_initiallySmall D t c hc f hf

end EssentiallySmall

end AlgebraicGeometry
